<article class="env-lemma" id="09Q7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09Q7">Lemma <span data-tag="09Q7">23.8.9</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a flat local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. Then the following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$B$ is a complete intersection, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$A$ and $B/\mathfrak m_ A B$ are complete intersections. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Now that the definition makes sense this is a trivial reformulation of the (nontrivial) Proposition <a href="/tag/09Q2" data-tag="09Q2">23.8.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>